From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Blacklist the remaining emSign roots

Mozilla's root list no longer has "emSign Root CA - C1" and
"emSign ECC Root CA - C3". It limits "emSign Root CA - G1" to TLS
certificates issued up to a date, which a PEM bundle can't express.
---
 mozilla/blacklist.txt | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/mozilla/blacklist.txt
+++ b/mozilla/blacklist.txt
@@ -7,5 +7,11 @@
 "emSign ECC Root CA - G3"
 # Blacklist "Comodo AAA Services root" (cf. #1151413)
 "Comodo AAA Services root"
+# Blacklist the roots that Mozilla's list no longer has
+"emSign Root CA - C1"
+"emSign ECC Root CA - C3"
+# Mozilla and Chrome limit this one to certificates issued up to a date,
+# which a PEM bundle can't express
+"emSign Root CA - G1"
 
 # Expired CAs
